From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32, gdiplus: IShellImageData and its factory, encoder parameter lists (3685)

shell32, gdiplus: IShellImageData and its factory, encoder parameter lists

IShellImageData now answers for the loaded picture: pages and frames
(NextFrame, NextPage, PrevPage, SelectPage, page count and current page),
IsTransparent, IsAnimated, IsVector, IsMultipage, IsEditable, IsPrintable,
IsDecoded, the raw and pixel formats, the frame delay, size and resolution,
Rotate and Scale (with DiscardEdit to go back), the display name,
CloneFrame and ReplaceFrame. The factory creates an empty object, an object
for a stream, and tells the data format of a file. gdiplus gets
GdipGetEncoderParameterList and GdipGetEncoderParameterListSize for the
JPEG, TIFF and GIF encoders (Transformation, Quality, tables, Compression,
ColorDepth, SaveFlag), which IShellImageData::GetEncoderParams returns.

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto 3258 (fast-a): ShellImageData struct/creation/release from 3685 (superset); SetEncoderParams keeps 3258's body (AddRef before Release, mutant SG_MUTANT_SID_ENCPARAMS).
